:: Whitney Locker Game Intro
<<effects>>
<<set $weekly.whitneyLockerGame to true>>
<<set $daily.whitney.lockerGame to true>>
<<if $whitneyromance is 1 and ![1,2].includes($whitney_orphanage_special_seen)>>
	Whitney grabs your shoulder as you pass <<him>> in the corridor. Before you can ask what <<he>> wants,
	<<he>> pulls you through the stairwell door and lets it bang shut behind you.
	<br><br>
	"Hide and seek," <<he>> says. You start to smile, and <<he>> jabs a finger at your face. "Don't laugh! I'm not joking.
	You hide, I find you. If I find you, I pick what happens at lunch. If I don't..."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> stops and glares up the stairs as if the answer is written on the ceiling. "I'll buy you lunch.
	It's a dare! From me to you. So are you in or what?"
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Play|Whitney Locker Game Hide]]>><<set $phase to 0>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Tell Whitney you'd rather not|Whitney Locker Game Refuse]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	A hand slams against the wall beside your head before you can turn the corner.
	Whitney's friends fan out behind <<him>> and take up so much of the corridor that
	everyone else starts walking around the group.
	<br><br>
	"Game time," Whitney says. "Hide and seek. You hide, I seek. Ten seconds' head start, because I'm generous."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> glances over <<his>> shoulder at the others. "If I find you, you're mine at lunch.
	If I don't, you're off the hook. Easy."
	<br><br>
	One of the friends laughs. Whitney looks back at you. "And if I get bored, maybe I just leave you wherever you hid."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Play|Whitney Locker Game Hide]]>><<set $phase to 1>><<stress 3>><</link>><<gstress>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Refuse|Whitney Locker Game Refuse]]>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Whitney Locker Game Refuse
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if $whitneyromance is 1 and ![1,2].includes($whitney_orphanage_special_seen)>>
	<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
		You loosen your arm instead of pulling away and wait until Whitney lets go. "I'd rather not play."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		You shake your head. "No, thanks. I'd rather do something else."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "neutral" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
		You pull your shoulder free. "Not today."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
		"Find someone else to boss around." You pull your shoulder free.
		<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>"I'm not entertaining you just because you're bored."<</if>>
	<<else>>
		You pull your sleeve free. "I'd rather not."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	Whitney's hand drops to <<his>> side. "Boring," <<he>> says, but <<he>> lets you move away without grabbing you again.
	<br><br>
	<<He>> turns towards the stairs. "Another time, then."
	<br><br>
	Whitney takes the stairs two at a time. As <<he>> turns at the landing,
	<span class="pink">the tips of <<his>> ears have gone red</span>.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Hallways]]>><<endevent>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
		You take a step back. "I don't want to."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
		You keep your arms close to your sides while Whitney's friends watch. "I don't want to play."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		You move away from the wall. "No, thanks. I'm going to class."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "neutral" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
		You step away from Whitney's hand against the wall. "No. I'm not playing."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
		"Not happening." You turn to face Whitney properly.
		<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>"Go find somebody who cares."<</if>>
	<<else>>
		You step away from the wall. "No."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<if C.npc.Whitney.love gte random(10, 20)>>
		Whitney rolls <<his>> eyes. "Spoilsport."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> jerks <<his>> chin at the others, and they drift away from the corridor to leave you room to pass.
		"Fine. Another time, then."
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Next|Hallways]]>><<endevent>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		Whitney steps into your path again. "Wasn't a question."
		<br><br>
		The friends close in from both sides until there is no clear way through them.
		Whitney raises one hand and starts counting on <<his>> fingers. "Ten. Nine. Eight..."
		<br><br>
		Someone shoves you between the shoulder blades. You stumble forward, and Whitney laughs. "Better run."
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Run|Whitney Locker Game Hide]]>><<set $phase to 1>><<def 1>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Whitney Locker Game Hide
<<effects>>
<<set _rom to ($whitneyromance is 1 and ![1,2].includes($whitney_orphanage_special_seen))>>
<<set $daily.whitney.lock to { spot: "", found: false, ev: "", res: 0, step: 0, heat: 0, cues: shuffle(["far", "lookout", "close"]) }>>
<<if _rom>>
	Whitney turns to the wall and covers <<his>> face with both hands. "One. Two. Three."
	<br><br>
	A gap opens between <<his>> fingers. You catch <<him>> peeking before <<he>> shuts it again.
	"Four, five... I wasn't looking. Move."
<<else>>
	Whitney turns around and starts counting far too loudly. "Ten! Nine!"
	<br><br>
	<<He>> glances back at the friends. "Seven."
	<br><br>
	One of them snorts. Whitney points down the corridor without turning to face you. "You should probably run."
<</if>>
<br><br>
There is nowhere to hide here. Whitney only has to turn round to see you, so you need to get out of sight first.
<br><br>
<<link [[Run|Whitney Locker Game Run]]>><<pass 2>><</link>>
<br>

:: Whitney Locker Game Run
<<effects>>
<<set _rom to ($whitneyromance is 1 and ![1,2].includes($whitney_orphanage_special_seen))>>
<<set _lock to $daily.whitney.lock>>
<<set _cue to _lock.cues[_lock.step]>>
<<switch _lock.step>>
	<<case 0>>
		You bolt down the nearest corridor, away from the counting. It follows you anyway, bouncing off the lockers.
	<<case 1>>
		You cut through the lower corridor, past the noticeboards and the trophy cabinet, keeping close to the wall.
	<<default>>
		You slip along the back of the building, where the corridor runs past the art rooms and the smell of paint thinner hangs in the air.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<switch _cue>>
	<<case "far">>
		<<if _rom>>
			Whitney's voice is still at the stairs, counting slowly and cheating by a second at every number. You have time to be careful.
		<<else>>
			You can still hear Whitney from the stairwell, shouting numbers and laughing with the others. Nobody is close. You have time to be careful.
		<</if>>
	<<case "lookout">>
		A hall monitor is standing at the corner ahead, clipboard against their chest, watching the corridor over the top of it.
		Running past them would turn every head in the building.
	<<default>>
		<<if _rom>>
			Footsteps come round the next corner, unhurried and getting louder. Whitney is whistling again, badly. There is no time to creep.
		<<else>>
			Footsteps and laughter come round the next corner, getting louder. The friends have split up, and one of them is almost on top of you.
			There is no time to creep.
		<</if>>
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<if _cue is "far">>
	<<set _sd to (_rom ? 100 : 300) + _lock.heat * 100>>
<<elseif _cue is "lookout">>
	<<set _sd to (_rom ? 300 : 500) + _lock.heat * 100>>
<<else>>
	<<set _sd to (_rom ? 500 : 700) + _lock.heat * 100>>
<</if>>
<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to _sd>>
<<athleticsdifficulty 1 600>>
<br>
<<link [[Keep low and move along the lockers|Whitney Locker Game Run Result]]>><<set $skulduggerydifficulty to _sd>><<skulduggerycheck "silent">><<set $daily.whitney.lock.act to "sneak">><<set $daily.whitney.lock.ok to ($skulduggerysuccess is 1)>><<pass 3>><</link>><<skulduggerydifficulty>>
<br>
<<link [[Sprint for the next corner|Whitney Locker Game Run Result]]>><<set $daily.whitney.lock.act to "sprint">><<set $daily.whitney.lock.ok to ($athleticsSuccess is 1 and _cue isnot "lookout")>><<pass 2>><<tiredness 1>><</link>><<gtiredness>>
<br>
<<link [[Duck into a doorway and let them pass|Whitney Locker Game Run Result]]>><<set $daily.whitney.lock.act to "doorway">><<set $daily.whitney.lock.ok to (random(1, 100) lte ((_cue is "far" ? 80 : (_cue is "lookout" ? 55 : 35)) + (_rom ? 10 : 0)))>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<br>

:: Whitney Locker Game Run Result
<<effects>>
<<set _rom to ($whitneyromance is 1 and ![1,2].includes($whitney_orphanage_special_seen))>>
<<set _lock to $daily.whitney.lock>>
<<set _cue to _lock.cues[_lock.step]>>
<<if _lock.act is "sneak">>
	<<if _lock.ok>>
		You slide along the lockers, stopping whenever a footstep sounds and moving again when it fades.
		By the time you reach the corner, the voices are behind you.
	<<else>>
		Your shoulder bumps a locker door, making the metal rattle loudly.
		<br><br>
		The whistling stops. <<if _rom>>"Heard that," Whitney calls.<<else>>"Over here!" someone shouts.<</if>>
		You are moving again before the footsteps start to run.
	<</if>>
<<elseif _lock.act is "sprint">>
	<<if _cue is "lookout">>
		"No running!" the hall monitor snaps. Every head in the corridor turns, and behind you somebody laughs.
		<br><br>
		<<if _rom>>"Found a clue," Whitney sing-songs from the stairs.<<else>>"That's <<phim>>!" one of the friends yells.<</if>>
		You keep going, but there is no pretending now.
	<<elseif _lock.ok>>
		You break into a run and take the corner on your toes. Nobody calls after you.
	<<else>>
		Your shoe squeaks on the polished floor and you slide into a noticeboard, sending a pin skittering across the tiles.
		<br><br>
		<<if _rom>>"Oh, I definitely heard that," Whitney calls. The voice is closer than before.<<else>>"I hear you!" Whitney calls.
		The voice is closer than before.<</if>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<if _lock.ok>>
		You slip into the doorway of an empty classroom and hold your breath. The footsteps pass the glass, slowly, and fade.
		You wait until you can't hear them any more before you move again.
	<<else>>
		The door handle squeaks under your hand. The footsteps stop right outside.
		<br><br>
		You slip out through the other door before the first one opens.
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<if !_lock.ok>>
	<<set $daily.whitney.lock.heat to _lock.heat + 1>>
<</if>>
<<set $daily.whitney.lock.step to _lock.step + 1>>
<br><br>
<<if $daily.whitney.lock.heat gte 2>>
	<<link [[Next|Whitney Locker Game Result]]>><<set $daily.whitney.lock.found to true>><<set $daily.whitney.lock.spot to "run">><<pass 3>><</link>>
<<elseif $daily.whitney.lock.step lt 3>>
	<<link [[Keep moving|Whitney Locker Game Run]]>><<pass 2>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Look for somewhere to hide|Whitney Locker Game Spot]]>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Whitney Locker Game Spot
<<effects>>
<<set _rom to ($whitneyromance is 1 and ![1,2].includes($whitney_orphanage_special_seen))>>
<<set _heat to $daily.whitney.lock.heat>>
<<set _bonus to _heat * 15>>
<<if _heat is 0>>
	You have put a few corridors between you and the search. For the moment nobody is looking at you,
	and you can hear the hunt starting up again somewhere far behind.
<<else>>
	You are still ahead of the search, but not by much. The footsteps behind you have not gone away.
<</if>>
There are a few places nearby where you might fit. Where do you hide?
<br><br>
<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to (_rom ? 300 : 500) + _heat * 100>>
<<link [[Inside a locker|Whitney Locker Game Search]]>><<set $skulduggerydifficulty to (_rom ? 300 : 500) + _heat * 100>><<skulduggerycheck "silent">><<set $daily.whitney.lock to { spot: "locker", found: $skulduggerysuccess isnot 1, ev: "", res: 0 }>><<pass 5>><</link>><<skulduggerydifficulty>>
<br>
<<link [[In the art room cupboard|Whitney Locker Game Search]]>><<set $daily.whitney.lock to { spot: "cupboard", found: random(1, 100) lte ((_rom ? 35 : 55) + _bonus), ev: "", res: 0 }>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Behind the stage curtains in the hall|Whitney Locker Game Search]]>><<set $daily.whitney.lock to { spot: "curtain", found: random(1, 100) lte ((_rom ? 40 : 60) + _bonus), ev: "", res: 0 }>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Among the crowd by the canteen doors|Whitney Locker Game Search]]>><<set $daily.whitney.lock to { spot: "crowd", found: random(1, 100) lte ((_rom ? 50 : 30) + _bonus), ev: "", res: 0 }>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<br>

:: Whitney Locker Game Search
<<effects>>
<<set _rom to ($whitneyromance is 1 and ![1,2].includes($whitney_orphanage_special_seen))>>
<<set _lock to $daily.whitney.lock>>
<<switch _lock.spot>>
	<<case "locker">>
		You squeeze into the locker sideways. A PE bag fills most of the bottom,
		so you push it behind your ankles and pull your knees in until the door can close.
		<br><br>
		Thin strips of corridor show through the vents.
		You can watch people pass without pressing your face against the metal.
	<<case "cupboard">>
		You slip into the room and pull open the storage cupboard.
		A bundle of poster tubes starts to roll off the shelf, and you catch it just before it hits the floor.
		Once it is steady, you squeeze in between two stacks of boxes.
		<br><br>
		With your feet tucked in, you pull the door almost shut and leave a narrow gap for air.
	<<case "curtain">>
		You hurry into the hall and duck behind the stage curtain.
		There is barely any room between the fabric and the wall, so you turn sideways to fit.
		Once you are hidden, you tug the bottom edge across your shoes.
		<br><br>
		You keep one hand on the curtain so it can't swing back and show you up.
	<<default>>
		You head for the canteen doors instead of trying to vanish into a room.
		A loose crowd has gathered there, and you work your way between two taller students
		before slowing down to match everyone around you.
		<br><br>
		You face the doors and pretend you have been waiting there all along.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Whitney Locker Game Search 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Whitney Locker Game Search 2
<<effects>>
<<set _rom to ($whitneyromance is 1 and ![1,2].includes($whitney_orphanage_special_seen))>>
<<set _lock to $daily.whitney.lock>>
<<if !_lock.ev>>
	<<set _evNow to ["promise", "teacher"].random()>>
	<<set $daily.whitney.lock.ev to _evNow>>
	<<set $daily.whitney.lock.teacher to ["Winter", "Sirris", "Doren", "Leighton"].random()>>
<<else>>
	<<set _evNow to _lock.ev>>
<</if>>
<<if _rom>>
	Whitney comes along the corridor whistling badly on purpose. "Where are you? I'm not looking.
	I'm not even in the building!"
	<br><br>
	A locker door bangs shut nearby. Whitney keeps walking, opening doors and checking corners one by one.
<<else>>
	Whitney's voice carries from further down the corridor while the friends spread out to search. "Come out, <<bitch>>.
	We're not going to hurt you!"
	<br><br>
	Someone laughs. Whitney adds, "Much."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if _evNow is "promise">>
	<<if _rom>>
		The searching stops close by. "All right, you win," Whitney says. "Come out and I won't make you do anything. Scout's honour."
		<br><br>
		There is a pause. "I mean it. Scout's honour."
	<<else>>
		Whitney tells the others to stop, and their footsteps go quiet one after another.
		"Fine, you win. Come out now and we'll call it off. No forfeit. Swear down."
		<br><br>
		Nobody else answers. Somewhere nearby, one of the friends snorts, and somebody shushes them.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Stay hidden|Whitney Locker Game Result]]>><<set $daily.whitney.lock.res to 1>><<pass 5>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Believe <<him>> and come out|Whitney Locker Game Result]]>><<set $daily.whitney.lock.res to 2>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<set _tn to $daily.whitney.lock.teacher>>
	A classroom door opens further down the corridor. <<npc _tn 2>><<person2>><<print _tn>> steps out and folds <<his>> arms.
	"What are you lot doing here? Shouldn't you be in lessons?"
	<br><br>
	<<if _rom>>
		Whitney stops almost at once. "Looking for a lost book," <<person1>><<he>> says,
		in a voice so flat it sounds worse than the truth.
		<br><br>
		<<print _tn>> starts asking where Whitney last had it, and Whitney answers without moving from the spot.
	<<else>>
		The friends stop opening doors. One of them laughs a little too brightly. "Just chatting."
		<br><br>
		<<print _tn>> keeps them there and starts asking why none of them are in class.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Keep quiet and wait|Whitney Locker Game Result]]>><<set $daily.whitney.lock.res to 1>><<pass 5>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Make a small noise on purpose|Whitney Locker Game Result]]>><<set $daily.whitney.lock.res to 2>><<stress 3>><<pass 5>><</link>><<gstress>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Whitney Locker Game Result
<<effects>>
<<set _rom to ($whitneyromance is 1 and ![1,2].includes($whitney_orphanage_special_seen))>>
<<set _lock to $daily.whitney.lock>>
<<set _found to (_lock.found or (_lock.ev is "promise" and _lock.res is 2) or (_lock.ev is "teacher" and _lock.res is 2))>>
<<if _lock.ev is "promise" and _lock.res is 2>>
	You leave your hiding place carefully and look both ways before stepping out.
	<br><br>
	Whitney appears from around the corner almost at once, with both hands in <<his>> pockets and a grin already waiting for you.
	"Told you I wasn't looking," <<he>> says as <<he>> walks up. "Didn't say I wasn't lying."
	<br><br>
	<<if !_rom>>
		Two of the friends come out through the side doors behind <<him>>, and another steps out from near the stairs.
	<<else>>
		Whitney is still smiling when <<he>> looks back at you, but the expression fades once <<he>> sees your face.
		<br><br>
		<<He>> pauses for a moment, then looks towards the stairs instead. "You actually came out."
	<</if>>
<<elseif _lock.ev is "teacher" and _lock.res is 2>>
	You make a small noise while the teacher waits for an answer. <<print _lock.teacher>> stops talking. "Who's that?"
	<br><br>
	Footsteps come towards you. By the time you are found,
	Whitney is following a few steps behind <<print _lock.teacher>> with a badly hidden grin.
<<elseif _found>>
	<<switch _lock.spot>>
		<<case "locker">>
			The locker handle rattles. You pull your legs in tighter,
			but the door opens and light from the corridor falls across you.
			<br><br>
			Whitney taps the number sticker with one finger. "Nineteen. Found you."
		<<case "cupboard">>
			The cupboard door opens a few inches, catches on your knee, and swings wider when you shift back.
			Whitney reaches past an easel and takes hold of your sleeve.
			<br><br>
			"Hello, slut," <<he>> says, tugging you towards the door.
		<<case "curtain">>
			A hand grabs the edge of the curtain and pulls it aside. Whitney looks down first, then up at you.
			"Nice try. Your shoes were sticking out."
		<<case "run">>
			<<if _rom>>
				You round the corner and walk straight into Whitney, who was waiting beside the door with <<his>> arms folded.
				<br><br>
				"You're a terrible runner," <<he>> says, catching your elbow. "I could hear you from the stairs."
			<<else>>
				You round the corner and find two of the friends blocking the corridor, with Whitney strolling up behind them.
				"Told you I'd hear you. You run like a duck."
			<</if>>
		<<default>>
			A hand lands on your shoulder from behind. You turn round and find Whitney standing much too close.
			"You've been standing here for five minutes. Nobody in this queue has moved once."
	<</switch>>
<<else>>
	<<if _rom>>
		Whitney passes your hiding place once, doubles back, and passes it again.
		A few minutes later the searching stops altogether.
		<br><br>
		You hear <<him>> drop onto the bottom stair. "Fine! You win. Come out. I'm done."
		<br><br>
		You wait until <<he>> says it a second time before leaving your hiding place.
		Whitney stays sitting there, looking annoyed at the floor instead of at you.
	<<else>>
		The footsteps move further away until you can't hear them any more. The bell rings,
		but Whitney and the others still don't come back.
		<br><br>
		You wait several more minutes before risking a look outside. The corridor is empty.<<pass 13>>
		<br><br>
		By the time you step out, you are late for class,
		and you can hear Whitney laughing somewhere near the far stairs.
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Whitney Locker Game Result 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Whitney Locker Game Result 2
<<effects>>
<<set _rom to ($whitneyromance is 1 and ![1,2].includes($whitney_orphanage_special_seen))>>
<<set _lock to $daily.whitney.lock>>
<<set _found to (_lock.found or (_lock.ev is "promise" and _lock.res is 2) or (_lock.ev is "teacher" and _lock.res is 2))>>
<<if _found>>
	<<if _rom>>
		Whitney checks both ends of the corridor before facing you again.
		<<He>> shoves <<his>> hands deeper into <<his>> pockets. "I get to pick. That was the deal."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> takes one step towards you. "Come here."
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Go to <<him>>|Whitney Locker Game End]]>><<set $phase to 1>><<pass 5>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Stay where you are and make <<him>> ask|Whitney Locker Game End]]>><<set $phase to 2>><<pass 5>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Say you'd rather call it a draw|Whitney Locker Game End]]>><<set $phase to 3>><<pass 5>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		Whitney grabs the front of your clothes and pulls you out where the friends can see.
		You have to take two quick steps to keep your balance.
		<br><br>
		"Mine at lunch," <<he>> tells them. "Everyone heard the rules."
		<br><br>
		One of the friends starts laughing. Whitney looks back at you, waiting to see what you do.
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Go quietly|Whitney Locker Game End]]>><<set $phase to 1>><<stress 6>><<sub 1>><<pass 10>><</link>><<gstress>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Pull free and glare|Whitney Locker Game End]]>><<set $phase to 2>><<def 1>><<pass 5>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<if Transformations.partActive("traits", "fangs")>>
			<<link [[Bare your teeth|Whitney Locker Game End]]>><<set $phase to 3>><<pass 5>><</link>><<note "Fangs" "gold">>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Next|Whitney Locker Game End]]>><<set $phase to 0>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Whitney Locker Game End
<<effects>>
<<set _rom to ($whitneyromance is 1 and ![1,2].includes($whitney_orphanage_special_seen))>>
<<set _lock to $daily.whitney.lock>>
<<set _found to (_lock.found or (_lock.ev is "promise" and _lock.res is 2) or (_lock.ev is "teacher" and _lock.res is 2))>>
<<if !_found>>
	<<if _rom>>
		<<set $daily.whitney.lunchDeal to "treat">>
		Whitney stays on the bottom stair a moment longer, then gets up and brushes the dust off <<his>> clothes without looking at you.
		"Lunch is on me. Canteen, table by the window. Don't be late!"
		<br><br>
		<<Hes>> already climbing the stairs before you can answer.
	<<else>>
		Whitney is waiting outside the canteen with the same friends from earlier.
		"Where were you? We looked everywhere."
		<br><br>
		Nobody believes the innocent tone, including Whitney. <<He>> smiles. "Good news.
		I'm in a good mood, so you're off this time."
		<br><br>
		One of the friends raises a phone towards you.
		<br><br>
		You turn your face away before they can line up the shot and keep walking.
		You still reach the next lesson late, and the teacher writes your name down.<<detention 1>><<gdelinquency>>
	<</if>>
<<elseif _rom>>
	<<switch $phase>>
		<<case 1>>
			<<set $daily.whitney.lunchDeal to "forfeit">>
			You walk over to Whitney. <<He>> looks past you to make sure nobody is coming,
			then grabs the front of your clothes and pulls you in until your noses almost touch.
			"Lunch! Table by the window. You're sitting with me for the whole thing."
			<br><br>
			<<He>> lets go and steps back, wiping a hand across <<his>> mouth as if that was the part that embarrassed <<him>>.
			"Don't look at me like that. Just be there."
			<br><br>
			Whitney heads for class before you can answer, walking too fast, with blush still in <<his>> face when you reach the corridor.
			<<npcincr Whitney love 1>><<npcincr Whitney lust 5>><<glove>><<glust>>
		<<case 2>>
			<<speechresolve>>
			<<set $daily.whitney.lunchDeal to "forfeit">>
			<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
				You stay where you are and rub your thumb across your opposite wrist. "Could you ask me properly?"
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
				You stay in place instead of making Whitney come after you. "Could you ask me properly?"
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				You shake your head. "Ask nicely, please."
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "neutral">>
				You fold your arms. "Ask nicely."
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				You stay where you are. "You can ask properly."
				<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">> "Go on. Try again."<</if>>
			<<else>>
				You stay where you are. "Ask nicely."
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
			Whitney starts to snap back, but stops and pulls one hand out of <<his>> pocket. "Fine. Please."
			<br><br>
			<<He>> holds the hand out. "Please come here and sit with me at lunch. Happy?"
			<br><br>
			You take <<his>> hand, and <<he>> pulls you into the corner of the stairwell.
			<br><br>
			Whitney keeps hold of you long enough for <<his>> forehead to rest against yours.
			Then <<he>> looks down at your joined hands and steps back. "Table by the window! Don't be late." <<npcincr Whitney love 1>><<glove>>
		<<default>>
			<<speechresolve>>
			<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
				"Could we call it a draw?" you ask.
			<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
				You keep your hands by your sides. "Could we call it a draw?"
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
				"How about we call it a draw?" you ask.
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "neutral" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
				"Let's call it a draw," you say.
			<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
				"Call it a draw and quit while you're ahead," you say.
			<<else>>
				"Let's call it a draw," you say.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
			Whitney studies you for a second. "A draw," <<he>> repeats, scratching the side of <<his>> neck.
			"Yeah. Okay."
			<br><br>
			<<He>> holds out a hand, and you shake it before <<he>> can turn the whole thing into another argument.
			<<stress -3>><<lstress>>
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>
	<<if _lock.ev is "teacher" and _lock.res is 2>>
		<<print _lock.teacher>> points down the corridor and tells both of you to get to class.
		<<person1>>Whitney goes first, walking so quickly that you can still see the red in <<his>> ears from behind.
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<switch $phase>>
		<<case 1>>
			<<set $daily.whitney.lunchDeal to "bully">>
			You go with Whitney rather than fight in the corridor.
			"Lunch," <<he>> says, loud enough for everyone nearby to hear. "You're carrying my tray.
			Don't make me come and find you again."
			<br><br>
			The friends laugh as <<he>> walks off, and a few students look away from you a little too quickly.
		<<case 2>>
			<<set $daily.whitney.lunchDeal to "bullyHard">>
			You grab Whitney's wrist and pull <<his>> hand off your clothes.
			Once you have some room, you step back and make <<him>> come to you if <<he>> wants another go.
			<br><br>
			Whitney looks at <<his>> empty hand, then closes the gap again. "Oh, you want to do this here?"
			<br><br>
			<<He>> keeps coming until the lockers are pressed against your back.
			"I can make lunch a lot worse than carrying a tray. I'm doing you a favour."
			<br><br>
			Whitney points towards the canteen. "Don't be late!"
			<br><br>
			The friends move aside, laughing, and the students stuck behind them can finally use the corridor again.
		<<default>>
			You bare your teeth at Whitney, letting the warning show before you say anything.
			When <<he>> opens <<his>> mouth to make another joke, you growl and show your fangs, cutting <<him>> off.
			<br><br>
			The nearest friend stops laughing. Whitney lets go of your clothes and takes half a step back. "Fuck."
			<br><br>
			<<He>> points at your mouth while looking at the others. "Did you see that?! Fucking fangs!"
			<br><br>
			Whitney decides the game is over and leaves with them without mentioning lunch again.
			<<npcincr Whitney lust 5>><<glust>>
	<</switch>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<unset $daily.whitney.lock>>
<<link [[Next|Hallways]]>><<endevent>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Whitney Lunch Deal
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<set _lunch to $daily.whitney.lunch>>
<<switch _lunch>>
	<<case "treat">>
		Whitney slides the tray across to you with two fingers, as if handing over something <<he>> found on the floor.
		<<He>> has bought <<himself>> the same meal and is stabbing at it before you have sat down.
		<br><br>
		"Don't get smug," <<he>> says. "I lost, so I'm paying up. Doesn't mean anything."
		<br><br>
		A few students glance over from the next table. Whitney glares at the nearest one until they turn back round.
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Thank Whitney|Whitney Lunch Deal End]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Tease <<him>> about losing|Whitney Lunch Deal End]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Tear your bread roll in half and offer <<him>> a piece|Whitney Lunch Deal End]]>><<set $phase to 3>><</link>>
	<<case "forfeit">>
		Whitney drags <<his>> tray into the space between you and sets the fork down across it.
		<br><br>
		"You lost, so I get to decide the rules," <<he>> says. "You eat what I give you,
		and you stay where I can see you until we're done. That's your forfeit."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> cuts a bite from the sponge and spears it with the fork. Before holding it out to you,
		<<he>> glances around the room to make sure nobody nearby is paying attention.
		<br><br>
		"Come on." <<He>> brings the fork closer to your mouth,
		but looks away as soon as you notice what <<hes>> doing. "Eat it before someone sees me feeding you."
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Eat it off the fork|Whitney Lunch Deal End]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Take the fork and feed <<him>> instead|Whitney Lunch Deal End]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
	<<case "bully">>
		You carry Whitney's tray to the table while the friends watch. Whitney drops into <<his>> chair,
		props <<his>> boots on the next seat, and waits.
		<br><br>
		"Put it down. Not there." <<He>> taps the spot in front of <<him>>.
		You set the tray where <<he>> wants it, and <<he>> still doesn't touch it.
		"Now ask if I need anything else. Properly."
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Do as <<he>> says|Whitney Lunch Deal End]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Keep quiet and stand there|Whitney Lunch Deal End]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
	<<default>>
		Whitney has stacked two trays on the table in front of you and is already eating from the one nearest <<him>>.
		"You thought glaring would do something?" <<he>> says through a mouthful.
		"Pick them up, <<bitch>>. Both. And you can eat standing."
		<br><br>
		The friends spread out around the table to watch, and one of them starts a timer on <<his>> phone.
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Hold the trays and stand there|Whitney Lunch Deal End]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Put the trays down and sit|Whitney Lunch Deal End]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
<</switch>>
<br>

:: Whitney Lunch Deal End
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<set _lunch to $daily.whitney.lunch>>
<<switch _lunch>>
	<<case "treat">>
		<<switch $phase>>
			<<case 1>>
				"Thanks," you say.
				<br><br>
				"Yeah, yeah." Whitney keeps <<his>> eyes on <<his>> plate. "Eat before it goes cold."
				<br><br>
				<<He>> doesn't look up again for a while, but the tips of <<his>> ears have gone red.
				<<npcincr Whitney love 1>><<glove>>
			<<case 2>>
				"Seeker of the year," you say.
				<br><br>
				Whitney throws a chip at your forehead. "Shut up. It's not my fault you picked a good spot."
				<br><br>
				<<Hes>> trying to stay angry, but <<his>> mouth keeps twitching,
				and in the end <<he>> laughs into <<his>> fork.
				<<npcincr Whitney love 1>><<npcincr Whitney lust 3>><<glove>><<glust>>
			<<default>>
				You tear your bread roll in half and push one piece across the table.
				<br><br>
				Whitney stares at it. "I don't want it." <<He>> takes it anyway and eats it in two bites.
				"It's all right, I guess."
				<br><br>
				<<He>> slides a packet of crisps over to your side without saying anything.
				<<npcincr Whitney love 2>><<glove>>
		<</switch>>
		<<stress -4>><<lstress>>
	<<case "forfeit">>
		<<switch $phase>>
			<<case 1>>
				You lean forward and take the sponge off the fork.
				<br><br>
				Whitney's eyes linger on your mouth for a moment before
				<<he>> looks down at <<his>> plate and pushes the fork into <<his>> food.
				<br><br>
				"That's it. That's all you get," <<he>> says, but <<he>> pushes the rest of the tray towards you anyway.
				<<npcincr Whitney love 1>><<npcincr Whitney lust 5>><<glove>><<glust>>
			<<default>>
				You take the fork, cut a corner off the sponge, and hold it out to <<him>>.
				"Your turn."
				<br><br>
				Whitney's mouth opens before <<he>> can stop it. When <<he>> realises, <<he>> swallows and glares.
				"That wasn't the deal. Do that again and I'll..."
				<br><br>
				"You'll what?" you ask.
				<br><br>
				"Shut up and give me the rest."
				<<npcincr Whitney love 1>><<npcincr Whitney lust 3>><<glove>><<glust>>
		<</switch>>
		<<stress -4>><<lstress>>
	<<case "bully">>
		<<switch $phase>>
			<<case 1>>
				"Do you need anything else, Whitney?" you ask.
				<br><br>
				"Good <<bitch>>."
				<<if $settings.watersportsEnabled>>
					<<set _follow to true>>
					Whitney kicks out the chair beside <<him>> without looking at you. "Sit. Eat. Don't talk."
					<br><br>
					You sit down, and the friends close in around the table.
				<<else>>
					Whitney turns back to <<his>> friends, and you stay beside <<his>> chair until <<he>> waves you away.
					Every time <<he>> asks for something, <<he>> waits until you say it again before letting the conversation move on.
					If you forget, one of the friends reminds you.
					<br><br>
					By the time lunch is nearly over, people at the nearby tables keep looking over.
					<br><br>
					Each time somebody turns your way, Whitney notices and grins.
				<</if>>
				<<status -3>><<lcool>><<trauma 3>><<gtrauma>><<npcincr Whitney dom 1>><<gdom>>
			<<default>>
				You say nothing and stay where you are.
				<br><br>
				Whitney waits through the silence, watching you before turning to the nearest friends
				and snapping <<his>> fingers to get their attention.
				"Take <<phim>> to the back of the room. <<pShe>> can eat standing."
				<br><br>
				You spend lunch against the wall beside the bins, watching the friends laugh at the table.
				Nobody brings you any food.
				<<def 1>><<stress 6>><<gstress>><<status -3>><<lcool>>
		<</switch>>
	<<default>>
		<<switch $phase>>
			<<case 1>>
				You pick up both trays and stand there, arms shaking a little under the weight.
				<br><br>
				Whitney eats slowly, and the friends keep the timer going. "Don't drop anything. It'll just be worse."
				<br><br>
				By the time <<he>> finishes, your arms ache and half the canteen has seen you stand there like a waiter.
				<<sub 1>><<stress 6>><<gstress>><<status -3>><<lcool>><<trauma 3>><<gtrauma>>
			<<default>>
				You put both trays down on the nearest table and sit.
				<br><br>
				Whitney's chair scrapes back. <<He>> leans over you until you can smell <<his>> cigarettes.
				"I told you to stand."
				<br><br>
				<<He>> takes your tray, slides most of it onto <<his>> own, and hands the empty one back.
				"You can have the crumbs. That's what you get for being cheeky."
				<<def 1>><<stress 6>><<gstress>><<npcincr Whitney dom 1>><<gdom>>
		<</switch>>
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<unset $daily.whitney.lunch>>
<<if _follow>>
	<<link [[Next|Canteen Lunch Whitney Fake Pee]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<canteenlunchoptions>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Whitney Home Restraint Start
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>><<npc Whitney>><<person1>>
<<set _rom to ($whitneyromance is 1 and ![1,2].includes($whitney_orphanage_special_seen))>>
<<set _hard to (C.npc.Whitney.dom gte 15)>>
<<set $daily.whitney.restraintPlayed to true>>
<<set $whitneyRestraint to {
	pose: "",
	reaction: "",
	photo: 0,
	prev: {
		leftarm: $leftarm,
		rightarm: $rightarm,
		leftleg: $leftleg,
		rightleg: $rightleg
	}
}>>
<<speechresolve>>
Whitney is flipping through games on the television when you notice the restraints beside <<his>> bed.
Several straps have been left in a loose pile on the floor, tangled together.
<br><br>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	You point at them. "Could we try those? Maybe a different position?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	You point at the restraints but keep your hands in your lap. "Could we try those?
	You can pick something different if you want."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite">>
	"Would you show me something else you can do with those?" you ask, pointing beside the bed.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant">>
	You point at the pile. "All right, what else have you got?"
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "neutral" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
	"What else can you do with those?" you ask.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	You nod at the restraints. "Come on. Show me what you can do."
	<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">> "Let's see if you actually know what you're doing."<</if>>
<<else>>
	"What else can you do with those?" you ask.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Whitney pauses the game and looks from you to the straps.
<<if _rom>>
	"These?" <<He>> sets the controller on the bed, then reaches down and pulls the tangled straps apart.
	"I was going to bring them up anyway, so don't start acting like this was your idea."
	<br><br>
	<<if _hard>>
		Whitney picks up two restraints and checks the buckles. "You choose what you want.
		If you stand there thinking all night, I'm choosing for you."
	<<else>>
		<<He>> turns one strap over to check where the padding sits. "You can change your mind.
		Just don't go telling people I begged you into it."
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	Whitney nudges the pile with <<his>> foot. "Still want to play dog?"
	<br><br>
	<<He>> bends down and picks up the first strap. "Huh. Pick something, then.
	Let's see how long you last before you start whining."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Fold your arms and legs in close|Whitney Home Restraint Apply]]>><<set $whitneyRestraint.pose to "frog">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Lie down and let Whitney bind your wrists to your ankles|Whitney Home Restraint Apply]]>><<set $whitneyRestraint.pose to "hogtie">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Bend over the chair|Whitney Home Restraint Apply]]>><<set $whitneyRestraint.pose to "chair">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Change your mind|Whitney Home Restraint Refuse]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Whitney Home Restraint Refuse
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<set _rom to ($whitneyromance is 1 and ![1,2].includes($whitney_orphanage_special_seen))>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	You shake your head before Whitney can start. "Sorry. I changed my mind."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	You shake your head and stay where you are. "I changed my mind. Can we leave it?"
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	You raise a hand. "Actually, I'd rather not. Put them away, please."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "neutral" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
	You stop Whitney before <<he>> gets any further. "No. I changed my mind."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	You point back at the floor. "Nah. Put them away."
	<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">> "I'm already bored."<</if>>
<<else>>
	You shake your head. "I changed my mind."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if _rom>>
	Whitney stops winding a strap around <<his>> hand. "Fine."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> drops it beside the bed, picks up the controller, and holds it out to you. "Was your idea anyway. Move over."
<<else>>
	Whitney snorts. "Knew you'd chicken out."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> kicks the restraints under the bed and drops back into the chair. "Don't stare at them next time."
<</if>>
<<unset $whitneyRestraint>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Whitney Home Hang]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Whitney Home Restraint Apply
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<set _r to $whitneyRestraint>>
<<set _rom to ($whitneyromance is 1 and ![1,2].includes($whitney_orphanage_special_seen))>>
<<set _hard to (C.npc.Whitney.dom gte 15)>>
<<set $leftarm to "bound">><<set $rightarm to "bound">><<set $leftleg to "bound">><<set $rightleg to "bound">>
Whitney shoves the controller and everything else out of the way,
then brings the restraints over and sorts them by length on the bed.
<br><br>
<<He>> looks at the position you chose.
<br><br>
<<switch _r.pose>>
	<<case "frog">>
		Whitney has you sit on the rug first. <<He>> bends one of your legs until your ankle rests beside your hip,
		buckles the padded strap, then does the same on the other side.
		<br><br>
		"Don't straighten them," <<he>> says when you shift. "I'm doing your arms next."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> brings your wrists together low in front of you and fastens them near your knees.
		When you try to adjust your balance, Whitney catches your shoulder before you tip sideways
		and sets you back in the middle of the rug.
	<<case "hogtie">>
		Whitney tells you to lie on your stomach across the bed.
		<br><br>
		<<He>> guides your arms behind your back and brings your wrists together,
		making sure they are not twisted awkwardly before fastening the buckle around them.
		<br><br>
		Your ankles are next. Whitney bends your knees, buckles the ankle straps together,
		and joins them to your wrists with a short strap.
		<br><br>
		You try to lower your legs once, but the strap stops them before your feet reach the bed.
		Whitney puts a hand between your shoulders to stop you twisting after them. "Yeah. That's the point."
	<<default>>
		Whitney drags the desk chair into the clear part of the room and turns it round.
		<<He>> tests it with both hands before telling you to bend over the back.
		<br><br>
		<<He>> fastens one wrist beside the front leg, then the other.
		Moving behind you, <<he>> straps your ankles to the rear legs and
		leaves enough space between your feet to keep the chair steady.
		<br><br>
		<<He>> gives the chair a hard shove. It shifts less than an inch.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Whitney Home Restraint Settle]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Whitney Home Restraint Settle
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<set _r to $whitneyRestraint>>
<<set _rom to ($whitneyromance is 1 and ![1,2].includes($whitney_orphanage_special_seen))>>
<<set _hard to (C.npc.Whitney.dom gte 15)>>
Once you are fully in position, Whitney goes back over the restraints.
<<He>> checks each buckle with <<his>> fingers and makes sure no strap has folded over itself.
<br><br>
<<if _rom>>
	"Too tight?" <<He>> presses two fingers under the strap nearest your wrist, then does the same at your ankle.
	<<if _hard>>
		"And answer properly. I'm not guessing."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<speechresolve>>
	<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
		You flex your fingers carefully. "No. I think they're okay."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
		You test the nearest strap with a small movement, then settle again. "They're fine."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		"They're fine, thanks," you say.
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "neutral" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
		You move one wrist enough to check. "Yeah. They're fine."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
		"They're fine. Stop fussing," you say.
		<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">> "I said I wanted to do this."<</if>>
	<<else>>
		"They're fine," you say.
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	Whitney circles you slowly, checking every buckle. When <<he>> reaches the last one,
	<<he>> gives it a hard pull and looks satisfied.
	"Look at you, couldn't even wait for me to come up with the idea."
<</if>>
<br><br>
You can feel where each strap is holding you now. Nothing has come loose,
but there is still enough give to test them if you want to.
<br><br>
<<link [[Stay still and see what Whitney does|Whitney Home Restraint Reaction]]>><<set $whitneyRestraint.reaction to "still">><<sub 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Test the restraints|Whitney Home Restraint Reaction]]>><<set $whitneyRestraint.reaction to "test">><<stress 3>><</link>><<gstress>>
<br>
<<link [[Tell Whitney to stop|Whitney Home Restraint Stop]]>><<set $whitneyRestraint.reaction to "stop">><</link>>
<br>
<<if Transformations.partActive("traits", "fangs")>>
	<<link [[Growl at Whitney|Whitney Home Restraint Reaction]]>><<set $whitneyRestraint.reaction to "growl">><</link>><<note "Fangs" "gold">>
	<br>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Whitney Home Restraint Reaction
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<set _r to $whitneyRestraint>>
<<set _rom to ($whitneyromance is 1 and ![1,2].includes($whitney_orphanage_special_seen))>>
<<set _hard to (C.npc.Whitney.dom gte 15)>>
<<switch _r.reaction>>
	<<case "still">>
		You stop adjusting your position and leave your arms and legs where Whitney put them.
		After a few seconds the pull of the straps feels more even,
		and you let go of the tension you had been using to fight them.
		<br><br>
		<<if _rom>>
			Whitney watches until <<hes>> sure you have settled. One strap has twisted against your skin,
			so <<he>> reaches over and straightens the padding with two fingers.
			<br><br>
			"There." <<He>> checks the buckle once more, then lets go. "That should stop you fucking with it."
			<br><br>
			You keep looking at <<him>>. Whitney notices and scowls.
			<br><br>
			"What?! I just don't want you moaning about it later."
		<<else>>
			Whitney points at you as soon as you stop moving. "See? You can behave when you try."
			<br><br>
			<<He>> gives your collar a short tug, then lets it go. "Knew there was a good dog in there somewhere."
		<</if>>
		<<npcincr Whitney lust 4>><<glust>>
